{"step_index":286,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T13:42:41Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. this window should not at the welcome page .. it must display after a user have  have the write to verify ahs log in to the system not to dispaly on teh welcome page  \n2. continue \n3.  on this part you should log in so that u can verify  the second screen shot ut should be at the center not at the corner as it is .  the third secreen l think its proper  to be on the welcome page .  is the AI asssintant wroking . it seems its halusinating . is there any access levels between admin ,officer , on that last screen shot . l think they should be diffent on one access and one does not access . lets correct that \n4. lets a light background which is professional .not dark blue \n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request**: Change the UI color scheme from dark navy/slate blue (`#0f172a`, `#1e293b`) to a **clean, professional light background** across the web application (not dark blue).\n- **Previous Requests Completed**:\n  - Relocated verification search card and result box from `index.html` (welcome page) to `dashboard.html` (authenticated console).\n  - Centered `login.html` horizontally and vertically in the middle of the viewport.\n  - Eliminated confusing secondary \"Access Portal Dashboard\" button on `index.html`, leaving a direct \"Sign In to Verify Credentials\" CTA.\n  - Retained public \"Cryptographic Block Stream\" on `index.html` for ledger transparency.\n  - Resolved AI Assistant hallucinations by connecting `AiFraudDetectionService.processUserQuery()` to real database queries (`QualificationRepository`).\n  - Differentiated access levels for `ROLE_VERIFIER`, `ROLE_INSTITUTION` (Officer), and `ROLE_ADMIN` (Admin) on both frontend and backend.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Files Modified & Verified with `mvn clean test` (All 35 tests passing)**:\n  - `src/main/java/com/devops/qvs/config/DataInitializer.java`: Seeded `verifier` account (`Verifier@12345`).\n  - `src/main/java/com/devops/qvs/controller/WebController.java`: `/verify` redirects to `/dashboard?tab=verifyTab`.\n  - `src/main/java/com/devops/qvs/service/AiFraudDetectionService.java`: Dynamic DB query without fake hardcoded institution names; explained RBAC matrix.\n  - `src/main/resources/templates/index.html`: Welcome page hero CTA updated; verification window removed.\n  - `src/main/resources/templates/dashboard.html`: Added `#roleScopeBanner`, verification console tab, and role-based tab hiding.\n  - `src/main/resources/templates/login.html`: Centered layout; role access matrix cards added.\n  - `src/main/resources/static/js/app.js`: Bearer token passing, role enforcement for revoking/audit logs, in-dashboard tab switching.\n  - `src/main/resources/static/css/style.css`: Added `.container` class.\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Elements Currently Styled with Dark Blue\nThe user specifically dislikes the dark blue elements. In `src/main/resources/static/css/style.css`:\n- `.top-announcement` (lines 43-50): `background: #0f172a;` (dark slate blue) -> Should be light clean grey/blue e.g. `#f1f5f9` or `#e2e8f0` with dark text `#334155`.\n- `.navbar` (lines 57-64): `background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95);` with white brand logo and `#cbd5e1` links -> Should be clean professional light white/slate (`background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); backdrop-filter: blur(10px); border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;`) with dark text (`color: #0f172a;`) and brand title dark.\n- `.hero-section` (lines 158-166): `background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% -20%, #1e293b 0%, #0f172a 100%); color: white;` -> This is the primary dark blue hero. Must be changed to a clean, modern enterprise light gradient, e.g. `linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fafc 0%, #edf2f7 100%)` or `radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, #f1f5f9 0%, #e2e8f0 100%)` with dark text (`#0f172a`), `#475569` description, and subtle glowing accent.\n- `.hero-bg-glow`: Currently blue glow on dark background -> Update to soft subtle light blue radial gradient.\n- `.hero-badge`: Update text and border for high contrast against light background (`background: #e0e7ff; color: #3730a3; border-color: #c7d2fe;`).\n- `.footer` (lines 1119-1123, 1160): `background: #0f172a; color: #94a3b8;` -> Update to professional light grey (`background: #f8fafc; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; color: #64748b;`) with dark link colors (`color: #334155; hover: #2563eb;`).\n- `.ai-chat-header` (line 915): `background: #0f172a;` -> Update to modern enterprise blue or clean indigo gradient (`background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2563eb, #1d4ed8);`).\n- `.crypto-proof-box` (line 528): `background: #0f172a;` -> Update to clean terminal dark slate (`#1e293b`) or subtle light code box (`background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; color: #0f172a;`) while keeping hash legible.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Working Directory: `C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system`\n- JDK Path: `C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\tools\\jdk-17.0.10+7`\n- Maven Path: `C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\tools\\apache-maven-3.9.6\\bin\\mvn.cmd`\n- Command prefix required for running builds:\n  `$env:JAVA_HOME = \"C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\tools\\jdk-17.0.10+7\"; $env:Path = \"$env:JAVA_HOME\\bin;C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\tools\\apache-maven-3.9.6\\bin;$env:Path\"; mvn ...`\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Modify `src/main/resources/static/css/style.css`**:\n   - Change `.top-announcement` to a light background (`#f1f5f9`), dark text (`#475569`), with strong tag in `#2563eb`.\n   - Change `.navbar` to